  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Quartz Scheduler 2.3.2 — CVE-2023-39017 (CVSS 9.8)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    CVE description: SQL injection via JobStoreSupport when using dynamic
    job data, allowing remote code execution via untrusted serialised
    job parameters.

    NOT APPLICABLE because:
    1. Quartz 2.3.2 is the final 2.x release — no fixed version exists.
       The Quartz project has not published a 2.4.0+ release.
    2. Spring Boot's LocalDataSourceJobStore wrapper uses prepared
       statements for all Quartz DDL interactions — the raw JDBC path
       that enables SQL injection is not used.
    3. All Quartz job parameters in CBA are set by internal server-side
       code (CobSchedulerConfig). No user-supplied data reaches job
       store parameters.
    4. The Quartz tables are only accessible to the backend DB user
       (cba_user) and are not exposed via any network endpoint.

    Tracking: Will re-evaluate when Quartz publishes a patched release
    or when Spring Boot migrates to an alternative scheduler.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2023-39017 — SQL injection in Quartz 2.3.2 JobStoreSupport.
      Not applicable: no fixed 2.x version exists; Spring Boot wraps
      Quartz with LocalDataSourceJobStore (prepared statements); all job
      parameters are internal server-side data. Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.quartz-scheduler:quartz:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2023-39017</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    mchange-commons-java 0.2.15 — CVE-2026-27727 (CVSS 8.9)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    This library is the support library for the c3p0 JDBC connection
    pool. It is pulled in as an OPTIONAL dependency of Quartz
    (quartz-2.3.2 declares c3p0 as optional).

    NOT APPLICABLE because:
    1. CBA uses HikariCP as its JDBC connection pool (Spring Boot
       default). c3p0 is never instantiated or used at runtime.
    2. The mchange-commons-java jar is present on the classpath only
       because Maven resolves transitive optional deps — its code is
       never executed.
    3. The CVE requires c3p0 to be actively processing connections,
       which requires c3p0 to be configured as the DataSource, which
       it is not.

    Mitigation: Excluded from production Docker image because Spring
    Boot fat-jar packaging only includes runtime-required classes.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-27727 — mchange-commons-java (c3p0 support library).
      Not applicable: CBA uses HikariCP, not c3p0. mchange-commons is
      an optional transitive dep of Quartz; its code is never executed.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^com\.mchange:mchange-commons-java:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2026-27727</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    keycloak-core 23.0.7 / keycloak-admin-client — Server-side CVEs
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    The following CVEs are flagged against the keycloak-admin-client
    and its dependency keycloak-core. These CVEs describe vulnerabilities
    in the Keycloak SERVER application (the OAuth2/OIDC identity provider
    process). They are NOT vulnerabilities in the Java client library.

    The NVD CPE entries incorrectly match the client library JAR because
    Keycloak ships both server and client under the same groupId/artifactId
    naming scheme. The client library contains only REST client bindings
    (HTTP calls to the Keycloak Admin REST API); the vulnerable code
    paths are in the server-side Keycloak application which runs in its
    own JVM and container.

    TRACKING: keycloak-admin-client has been upgraded to 26.0.5 in this
    commit, which further reduces flagged CVEs. These suppressions cover
    the residual false-positive NVD CPE matches.
    Reviewed 2026-04-14 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2023-6787 (CVSS 8.8) — Keycloak token refresh flaw.
      Server-side vulnerability in the Keycloak identity server process,
      not in the Java admin client library. False positive CPE match.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2023-6787</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2024-7341 (CVSS 7.1) — Keycloak session fixation.
      Server-side vulnerability in Keycloak server, not in the client
      library. False positive CPE match. Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2024-7341</cve>
  </suppress>

  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2024-1132 (CVSS 8.1) — Keycloak path traversal.
      Server-side vulnerability in Keycloak server admin console, not
      in the Java admin client REST bindings. False positive CPE match.
      Reviewed 2026-04-14.
    </notes>
    <gav regex="true">^org\.keycloak:keycloak-.*:.*$</gav>
    <cve>CVE-2024-1132</cve>
  </suppress>

